  "seedRoutineDescPushPullLegs": "Three sessions a week, each one a different half of what you do: the muscles you push with, the ones you pull with, and legs. The usual next step once a beginner program stops adding weight every session.",
  "@seedRoutineDescPushPullLegs": {
    "description": "What one of the programs the app ships is, shown on the screen that offers it and on the routine it lands as. Plain and factual — no marketing."
  },
  "seedRoutineDescUpperLower": "Four sessions a week, alternating the upper body and the lower. Each muscle is trained twice a week, and no single session has to cover everything.",
  "@seedRoutineDescUpperLower": {
    "description": "What one of the programs the app ships is, shown on the screen that offers it and on the routine it lands as. Plain and factual — no marketing."
  },
  "seedRoutineDescStartingStrength": "Mark Rippetoe's novice barbell program. Alternate two three-lift workouts three days per week and add weight each session.",
  "@seedRoutineDescStartingStrength": {
